WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.138
Azure ships a lot of help here, and Microsoft
is unusually candid about its limits.

2
00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:09.171
Azure Policy's FedRAMP initiative
reports compliant only for the

3
00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:13.351
settings it can test, which is a partial
view, not a verdict on a control.

4
00:00:13.351 --> 00:00:18.050
Results arrive on a daily cycle, so
closures lag the fix by up to a day.

5
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.723
Exceptions have a native
form with an expiry,

6
00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:23.975
and the book allows them only
from an approved request.

7
00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:27.452
Defender for Cloud adds
dashboards and exports,

8
00:00:27.452 --> 00:00:31.450
but an export only fires on
change, so silence isn't proof.

9
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.187
Resource Graph is the simple read path.

10
00:00:34.187 --> 00:00:36.430
So how do results reach the ticket queue?
